<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niigata</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niigata is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, at the mouth of the Shinano River, and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niigata-prefecture">Niigata Prefecture</a>. It was one of the five ports opened to foreign trade under the treaties of 1858, actually opening in 1869. It is the largest city on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s Sea of Japan coast.</p></div>
